# Trivy vulnerability suppressions.
# Every entry here must have a matching write-up in SECURITY.md explaining
# why there's no fix yet and a matching entry in .grype.yaml.
# Format: https://aquasecurity.github.io/trivy/latest/docs/configuration/filtering/#trivyignore
#
# Review dates below are when each entry should be re-checked against
# upstream — not a promise a fix will exist by then, just a forcing
# function so these don't silently go stale forever.

# --- Debian 12 (bookworm) base image — node:24.19.0-slim ---
# None of these are reachable through Hestia's own code: the only process
# that ever runs in the container is `node server.js` (see Dockerfile CMD).
# perl, gzip, mount, ncurses, and libacl are inherited OS packages that
# Hestia's application code never invokes. Debian hasn't shipped patched
# packages for bookworm yet as of 2026-08-09.

# CVE-2026-53615: util-linux family — integer overflow/wraparound
# Affects: bsdutils, libblkid1, libmount1, libsmartcols1, libuuid1, mount,
# util-linux, util-linux-extra (all one Debian source package)
# exp: 2026-09-20
CVE-2026-53615

# CVE-2025-69720: ncurses buffer overflow
# Affects: libtinfo6, ncurses-base, ncurses-bin
# exp: 2026-09-20
CVE-2025-69720

# CVE-2026-41992: gzip global buffer overflow
# exp: 2026-09-20
CVE-2026-41992

# CVE-2026-54369: libacl symlink traversal privilege escalation
# exp: 2026-09-20
CVE-2026-54369

# perl-base — 8 distinct CVEs (Perl core + Archive::Tar/Storable/IO::Compress)
# Hestia is a Node.js app; perl is never invoked at runtime.
# exp: 2026-09-20
CVE-2026-13221
CVE-2026-42496
CVE-2026-57433
CVE-2026-8376
CVE-2026-42497
CVE-2026-48962
CVE-2026-57432
CVE-2026-9538

# CVE-2023-45853: zlib integer overflow / heap buffer overflow
# exp: 2026-09-20
CVE-2023-45853

# --- npm's own bundled tooling (ships inside the base Node.js image) ---
# Confirmed via direct image inspection: these live under
# /usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/ — they are npm's own
# dependencies, not Hestia's (absent from /app/node_modules, the app's
# actual runtime tree). npm itself is never invoked at container runtime.
# Planned fix: strip the bundled npm CLI from the runtime image in the
# Dockerfile, which removes this whole category rather than waiting on
# npm's own upstream to bump these internally.

# CVE-2026-13149, CVE-2026-14257, CVE-2026-69152: brace-expansion DoS
# exp: 2026-08-23
CVE-2026-13149
CVE-2026-14257
CVE-2026-69152

# CVE-2026-69192: ip-address inconsistent IP parsing
# exp: 2026-08-23
CVE-2026-69192

# CVE-2026-59873, CVE-2026-59874: node-tar DoS (gzip bomb / malformed archive)
# exp: 2026-08-23
CVE-2026-59873
CVE-2026-59874

# CVE-2026-12151: undici DoS via unbounded memory
# exp: 2026-08-23
CVE-2026-12151
